<title>USA: House panel backs US airline ticket tax extension.</title>
<headline>House panel backs US airline ticket tax extension.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The House Ways and Means Committee on Wednesday approved a bill that would extend a 10 percent U.S. airline ticket tax through September 30.</p>
<p>In a voice vote, the committee approved a bill that extends the air transportation excise taxes that expired after Dec. 31, 1996. There were no amendments to the bill.</p>
<p>The Senate Finance Committee had approved a similar bill last week. The respective bills must now be approved by the full House and the full Senate.</p>
</text>
